WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.357
Pandas gives us two common ways to select rows and columns more precisely.

00:00:05.357 --> 00:00:09.172
loc works with labels and conditions.

00:00:09.172 --> 00:00:12.817
I loc works with integer positions.

00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:21.662
In the first example, loc keeps rows where the channel is web and returns only order I D and amount.

00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:27.302
The code communicates the meaning of the selection because it uses column names.

00:00:27.302 --> 00:00:34.072
In the second example, I loc selects rows and columns by their numeric positions.

00:00:34.662 --> 00:00:43.539
For analytical work, label-based selection is often easier to understand later because names describe the purpose of the

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:48.378
data. Position-based selection is still useful when location itself is important.
